1
00:00:01,067 --> 00:00:02,367
<i>It looks like they're
eliminating each other.</i>

2
00:00:02,500 --> 00:00:03,933
<i>Maybe they're just eliminating
those who turned against them.</i>

3
00:00:04,067 --> 00:00:05,033
<i> Goodbye, Liza.</i>

4
00:00:05,167 --> 00:00:06,800
<i>Major, positive.
We found someone here.</i>

5
00:00:06,933 --> 00:00:08,500
<i>She was salvaged,
it was done in the grassland.</i>

6
00:00:08,633 --> 00:00:10,600
<i>Liza! Let's take her
to the hospital!</i>

7
00:00:10,733 --> 00:00:12,100
<i>Liza, where are your companions?</i>

8
00:00:12,233 --> 00:00:13,100
<i> Quarry.</i>

9
00:00:13,233 --> 00:00:14,567
<i> This is the CCTV footage.</i>

10
00:00:14,700 --> 00:00:16,467
<i>These syndicates
are something else.</i>

11
00:00:16,600 --> 00:00:17,600
<i>Even their guns are customized.</i>

12
00:00:17,733 --> 00:00:18,633
<i> That's for you.</i>

13
00:00:18,767 --> 00:00:20,767
<i> Your wife is really so kind.</i>

14
00:00:20,900 --> 00:00:23,067
<i>I hope she'll be the key for me
to enter heaven.</i>

15
00:00:23,200 --> 00:00:24,367
<i> What is the meaning of this?</i>

16
00:00:24,500 --> 00:00:25,633
<i> Someone told us...</i>

17
00:00:25,767 --> 00:00:27,533
<i>the group we're looking for
is here.</i>

18
00:00:27,667 --> 00:00:29,333
<i> I got you, Berdugo.</i>

19
00:00:29,467 --> 00:00:30,900
<i> [GUN FIRING]</i>

20
00:00:31,033 --> 00:00:32,267
<i> Berdugo, surrender now!</i>

21
00:00:32,400 --> 00:00:33,667
<i> I'm out of bullets, Berdugo!</i>

22
00:00:33,800 --> 00:00:35,167
<i> At long last, we got him.</i>

23
00:00:35,333 --> 00:00:36,667
<i>Berdugo has finally been caught,</i>

24
00:00:36,800 --> 00:00:39,233
<i> led by Major Miguel Delgado.</i>

25
00:00:39,367 --> 00:00:40,967
<i> So, where is Berdugo now?</i>

26
00:00:41,100 --> 00:00:42,367
<i> We will now see the face...</i>

27
00:00:42,500 --> 00:00:44,567
<i> behind the name Berdugo.</i>

28
00:00:46,600 --> 00:00:48,867
<i> [OBB]</i>

29
00:01:03,067 --> 00:01:03,933
<i> In a few moments,</i>

30
00:01:04,067 --> 00:01:05,367
<i> Bolagos Police will reveal</i>

31
00:01:05,500 --> 00:01:07,000
<i> the true identity</i>

32
00:01:07,167 --> 00:01:09,167
<i>of the drug lord
known as Berdugo.</i>

33
00:01:09,300 --> 00:01:10,567
<i> Wrong...</i>

34
00:01:11,467 --> 00:01:13,933
<i> You caught the wrong man.</i>

35
00:01:14,067 --> 00:01:15,267
<i> Wrong.</i>

36
00:01:16,067 --> 00:01:18,033
<i>Berdugo was caught last night,
after...</i>

37
00:01:18,167 --> 00:01:19,633
Wrong.

38
00:01:19,767 --> 00:01:20,633
Wro...

39
00:01:20,767 --> 00:01:22,500
- It's not right...
- Are you okay?

40
00:01:22,633 --> 00:01:24,067
It's not right.

41
00:01:25,233 --> 00:01:27,067
It's not right!

42
00:01:27,500 --> 00:01:29,333
- What is it, Mom?
- It's not right.

43
00:01:30,600 --> 00:01:32,633
What's not right, Mom?

44
00:01:33,133 --> 00:01:36,367
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

45
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:41,667
Mom, why do you look
so agitated?

46
00:01:41,833 --> 00:01:45,300
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

47
00:01:46,833 --> 00:01:48,533
Wow! You lost to Major!

48
00:01:48,667 --> 00:01:49,667
You're done!

49
00:01:49,800 --> 00:01:50,767
Yes!

50
00:01:50,900 --> 00:01:53,200
You'll pay for what you did
to my family.

51
00:01:53,333 --> 00:01:54,800
[INDISTINCT CHATTER ON TV]

52
00:01:54,933 --> 00:01:56,867
Wait, I know this guy.
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

53
00:01:57,833 --> 00:01:59,467
This is the one I fought
with before.

54
00:01:59,600 --> 00:02:00,967
[GRUNTING]

55
00:02:01,100 --> 00:02:02,367
[THUDS]

56
00:02:02,500 --> 00:02:04,100
<i> You don't want to stop, huh?</i>

57
00:02:04,233 --> 00:02:05,767
<i> What's going on here, Matias?</i>

58
00:02:05,900 --> 00:02:07,133
<i>So, you really know each other?</i>

59
00:02:07,267 --> 00:02:09,200
<i> Matias is my business partner.</i>

60
00:02:09,333 --> 00:02:11,833
And Tomas knows him too.

61
00:02:11,967 --> 00:02:13,133
So that's why he's so arrogant,

62
00:02:13,267 --> 00:02:15,367
he's Berdugo.

63
00:02:15,533 --> 00:02:18,333
Wait, good thing that crook
didn't finish you off.

64
00:02:18,467 --> 00:02:20,267
He's ruthless, right?

65
00:02:21,133 --> 00:02:23,333
That's why Jin Ho's concern

66
00:02:23,467 --> 00:02:25,733
and fear for Liza won't go away.

67
00:02:26,667 --> 00:02:28,300
I wonder how's oppa now?

68
00:02:30,033 --> 00:02:32,233
He's surely still sad,

69
00:02:32,367 --> 00:02:33,867
but maybe...

70
00:02:34,000 --> 00:02:36,600
he's okay now since Berdugo
was caught.

71
00:02:36,733 --> 00:02:40,700
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

72
00:02:42,800 --> 00:02:43,900
No!

73
00:02:44,433 --> 00:02:47,333
No! I didn't expect you
to come today.

74
00:02:49,933 --> 00:02:50,767
Mom...

75
00:02:51,500 --> 00:02:53,967
I'm so sorry
for not being here lately.

76
00:02:54,567 --> 00:02:57,133
Tomas and I are just going
through something.

77
00:02:58,033 --> 00:03:00,267
Ah, but I'll tell
you everything, Mom.

78
00:03:00,833 --> 00:03:02,367
Ah, we can eat.

79
00:03:02,500 --> 00:03:04,367
Let's eat first, Mom, okay?

80
00:03:05,367 --> 00:03:06,600
Come on.

81
00:03:06,733 --> 00:03:08,200
[INDISTINCT CAHTTER ON TV]

82
00:03:08,333 --> 00:03:10,633
And you too, follow later, okay?

83
00:03:11,500 --> 00:03:13,033
I'll just prepare the food.

84
00:03:13,167 --> 00:03:17,167
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

85
00:03:27,900 --> 00:03:31,933
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

86
00:03:32,067 --> 00:03:34,100
<i> I'm out of bullets, Berdugo!</i>

87
00:03:34,233 --> 00:03:35,600
<i> We have no choice.</i>

88
00:03:36,733 --> 00:03:38,233
<i> You'll be caught.</i>

89
00:03:38,367 --> 00:03:39,767
<i> You'll become Berdugo.</i>

90
00:03:39,900 --> 00:03:41,400
<i> What?</i>

91
00:03:41,533 --> 00:03:44,800
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

92
00:03:46,333 --> 00:03:48,933
<i>You know what I can do
to your wife and child.</i>

93
00:03:49,067 --> 00:03:51,600
<i>They can live peacefully
even without you.</i>

94
00:03:51,733 --> 00:03:54,267
<i>If not, you'll all be buried
together</i>

95
00:03:54,433 --> 00:03:55,900
<i> if you betray me!</i>

96
00:03:56,033 --> 00:04:00,100
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

97
00:04:03,033 --> 00:04:05,233
<i>Make sure you fulfill
what you're saying.</i>

98
00:04:05,367 --> 00:04:09,433
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

99
00:04:13,833 --> 00:04:14,933
<i> Don't shoot!</i>

100
00:04:15,067 --> 00:04:16,533
<i> I don't want to die yet!</i>

101
00:04:16,667 --> 00:04:18,233
<i> I have a family!</i>

102
00:04:18,367 --> 00:04:19,867
<i>Surrender now, Berdugo!
[BRAZEN MUSIC PLAYING]</i>

103
00:04:20,500 --> 00:04:24,100
<i> You have nowhere to go.</i>

104
00:04:24,233 --> 00:04:26,133
<i> Put down your gun!</i>

105
00:04:26,267 --> 00:04:27,767
<i> Down!</i>

106
00:04:27,933 --> 00:04:31,233
[BRAZEN MUSIC CONTINUES]

107
00:04:31,367 --> 00:04:32,933
<i> There! Come!</i>

108
00:04:33,867 --> 00:04:35,433
<i> Thank God, you're here.</i>

109
00:04:35,567 --> 00:04:39,767
[♪BRAZEN MUSIC CONTINUES♪]

110
00:04:44,467 --> 00:04:45,467
<i> Quick, stand up.</i>

111
00:04:45,600 --> 00:04:47,233
<i> Come on, take him!</i>

112
00:04:47,367 --> 00:04:48,867
<i>- Yes, Sir.
- Walk, walk!</i>

113
00:04:49,000 --> 00:04:53,433
[BRAZEN MUSIC CONTINUES]

114
00:04:57,733 --> 00:05:00,067
<i>So, you've known Berdugo
for a long time.</i>

115
00:05:00,200 --> 00:05:01,567
<i> He's pure evil.</i>

116
00:05:01,733 --> 00:05:03,867
<i>He threatened me and my family.</i>

117
00:05:04,467 --> 00:05:05,867
<i>Even Andrew
and my mother in-law,</i>

118
00:05:06,000 --> 00:05:07,467
<i> he said he'd involve them.</i>

119
00:05:07,600 --> 00:05:10,267
<i>So, whatever he ordered
or asked,</i>

120
00:05:10,400 --> 00:05:11,767
<i> I just gave in.</i>

121
00:05:13,067 --> 00:05:16,533
<i> Recently, he liked my car.</i>

122
00:05:16,667 --> 00:05:17,900
<i>I couldn't do anything about it!</i>

123
00:05:18,033 --> 00:05:20,000
<i> I was so scared.</i>

124
00:05:20,133 --> 00:05:22,267
<i>Why didn't you report it
to us police?</i>

125
00:05:22,400 --> 00:05:24,533
<i>I didn't know
who to trust anymore.</i>

126
00:05:24,667 --> 00:05:26,600
<i> If he caught me,</i>

127
00:05:26,733 --> 00:05:29,433
<i>I might not have a family
to go home to.</i>

128
00:05:29,567 --> 00:05:30,567
<i> You know that.</i>

129
00:05:30,700 --> 00:05:31,967
<i> I heard from Andrew</i>

130
00:05:32,100 --> 00:05:35,300
<i>what he did to you
and your family.</i>

131
00:05:35,467 --> 00:05:37,967
<i>So why was he
at your wife's event?</i>

132
00:05:38,100 --> 00:05:40,633
<i> He wanted to ask for a favor.</i>

133
00:05:40,767 --> 00:05:44,800
<i>But his foreign henchman
messed up.</i>

134
00:05:44,933 --> 00:05:47,900
<i>That was the first time
I saw someone killed.</i>

135
00:05:48,633 --> 00:05:50,633
<i> I was so scared!</i>

136
00:05:50,767 --> 00:05:54,800
<i>That's why I'm so thankful
you came.</i>

137
00:05:54,933 --> 00:05:57,567
<i>I've been looking for that
Berdugo for a long time.</i>

138
00:05:57,700 --> 00:05:59,767
<i> People like him...</i>

139
00:05:59,900 --> 00:06:01,933
<i> go straight to hell.</i>

140
00:06:02,867 --> 00:06:04,833
<i> That man owes me big time,</i>

141
00:06:04,967 --> 00:06:08,367
<i>and he should be thankful
I didn't finish him off.</i>

142
00:06:08,533 --> 00:06:12,100
[SINISTER MUSIC PLAYING]

143
00:06:12,233 --> 00:06:13,533
<i> That's what you thought...</i>

144
00:06:13,667 --> 00:06:15,067
<i>because even when I was right in
front of you,</i>

145
00:06:15,200 --> 00:06:16,833
<i>you still couldn't do anything.</i>

146
00:06:16,967 --> 00:06:19,467
<i> Did you think I would stop?</i>

147
00:06:19,600 --> 00:06:21,467
<i> Cut off one of my arms,</i>

148
00:06:21,600 --> 00:06:24,733
<i>I can grow two back
in its place.</i>

149
00:06:28,733 --> 00:06:32,933
[HEAVY MUSIC PLAYING]

150
00:06:46,233 --> 00:06:50,267
[HEAVY MUSIC CONTINUES]

151
00:06:59,400 --> 00:07:00,700
I am sorry, Liza.

152
00:07:04,233 --> 00:07:05,533
You do not deserve this.

153
00:07:10,500 --> 00:07:12,167
I wanted to get my revenge.

154
00:07:15,233 --> 00:07:16,767
I wanted to kill Berdugo.

155
00:07:22,100 --> 00:07:23,400
He may not be dead.

156
00:07:24,733 --> 00:07:25,933
But, he is caught.

157
00:07:27,833 --> 00:07:29,333
And now...

158
00:07:29,467 --> 00:07:31,100
he will suffer in jail.

159
00:07:32,567 --> 00:07:35,633
His time there,
will be his punishment...

160
00:07:35,767 --> 00:07:37,967
for what he did to you.

161
00:07:38,100 --> 00:07:44,800
[HEAVY MUSIC CONTINUES]

162
00:07:44,933 --> 00:07:46,367
[SMOOCHES]

163
00:07:46,500 --> 00:07:50,567
[HEAVY MUSIC CONTINUES]

164
00:07:54,900 --> 00:07:56,167
I will miss you.

165
00:07:58,967 --> 00:08:00,900
I hope you are at peace now.

166
00:08:04,567 --> 00:08:06,533
I am sorry.

167
00:08:08,233 --> 00:08:10,967
Berdugo's happy days are over.

168
00:08:11,100 --> 00:08:12,133
That's right.

169
00:08:12,500 --> 00:08:15,267
Oh, Mom, we should celebrate.

170
00:08:15,400 --> 00:08:17,300
You know, you're really amazing,
Joey.

171
00:08:17,433 --> 00:08:18,933
You read my mind.

172
00:08:19,067 --> 00:08:21,767
That's what I wanted to do also,
to celebrate.

173
00:08:21,933 --> 00:08:24,267
Of course, I didn't just
take after Dad

174
00:08:24,400 --> 00:08:26,033
but from you too, Mom.

175
00:08:26,167 --> 00:08:27,500
Hey, you have to join us, okay?

176
00:08:27,633 --> 00:08:29,233
-What do you want me to prepare?
- Yes, what?

177
00:08:29,367 --> 00:08:30,467
Anything.

178
00:08:30,600 --> 00:08:31,567
Whatever you want!

179
00:08:31,700 --> 00:08:33,667
Hey, are you okay?

180
00:08:35,200 --> 00:08:39,633
[PHONE RINGING]

181
00:08:41,600 --> 00:08:43,000
Hello, Sis?

182
00:08:45,133 --> 00:08:46,967
Okay, fine, I'll be there soon.

183
00:08:48,600 --> 00:08:50,767
Sorry, I need to go
to the rest house.

184
00:08:51,633 --> 00:08:53,433
Maybe mom needs something.

185
00:08:54,400 --> 00:08:55,733
What? You're not joining
the party?

186
00:08:55,867 --> 00:08:56,767
You're leaving?

187
00:08:59,367 --> 00:09:01,767
Family is more important.

188
00:09:02,667 --> 00:09:05,767
Andrew, I hope your mom
gets better.

189
00:09:06,500 --> 00:09:09,233
And please give my regards
to Ma'am Yvette, okay?

190
00:09:09,367 --> 00:09:10,700
Okay.

191
00:09:11,700 --> 00:09:12,700
[PLEASANT MUSIC PLAYING]

192
00:09:12,833 --> 00:09:14,233
Joey...

193
00:09:14,833 --> 00:09:17,200
now that this issue
with Berdugo is over,

194
00:09:17,333 --> 00:09:19,900
you can focus on
healing your family.

195
00:09:21,100 --> 00:09:23,500
I know there are many
challenges, but...

196
00:09:24,267 --> 00:09:25,600
we need to forget.

197
00:09:26,167 --> 00:09:27,200
Honestly,

198
00:09:27,333 --> 00:09:30,433
it's impossible to forget
what happened.

199
00:09:30,600 --> 00:09:34,033
What's important
is we remember the lessons

200
00:09:34,167 --> 00:09:36,733
and our friendship,
the four of us, right?

201
00:09:36,867 --> 00:09:38,433
That we're solid.

202
00:09:42,200 --> 00:09:44,733
Okay, I'll see you around, Joey.

203
00:09:44,867 --> 00:09:46,000
Take care.

204
00:09:46,133 --> 00:09:48,167
Hey, keep in touch, okay?

205
00:09:50,333 --> 00:09:51,733
Take care, Andrew.

206
00:09:52,300 --> 00:09:53,700
Text me, okay?

207
00:09:53,833 --> 00:09:55,533
[CHUCKLE]

208
00:09:55,667 --> 00:09:57,233
Or call.

209
00:09:57,367 --> 00:09:58,967
Or videocall.

210
00:09:59,100 --> 00:10:05,667
[PLEASANT MUSIC CONTINUES]

211
00:10:07,967 --> 00:10:09,100
Follow up on the ballistic
report

212
00:10:09,233 --> 00:10:11,067
from the gun recovered from
Matias.

213
00:10:11,200 --> 00:10:12,433
Copy, Major.

214
00:10:13,700 --> 00:10:14,800
Major Delgado.

215
00:10:14,933 --> 00:10:15,667
Sir.

216
00:10:15,800 --> 00:10:17,333
For now, we have a strong case

217
00:10:17,467 --> 00:10:19,867
because we caught Berdugo
in the act.

218
00:10:20,000 --> 00:10:24,000
So, let's file
all possible charges.

219
00:10:24,133 --> 00:10:28,700
Include Mr. Limjoco's sworn
statement too,

220
00:10:28,833 --> 00:10:31,800
so he won't be able to get out.

221
00:10:33,867 --> 00:10:35,767
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

222
00:10:35,933 --> 00:10:37,733
Oh, why? Is there a problem?

223
00:10:38,433 --> 00:10:43,133
Sir, after all the time I spent
searching for Berdugo...

224
00:10:44,067 --> 00:10:46,500
it felt too easy to find him
right away.

225
00:10:47,167 --> 00:10:49,500
It's like he was too careless.

226
00:10:51,067 --> 00:10:52,567
He's not like that.

227
00:10:53,433 --> 00:10:54,300
Maybe.

228
00:10:54,433 --> 00:10:57,600
Or maybe he was overconfident.

229
00:10:58,367 --> 00:11:00,667
Nonetheless, we captured him.

230
00:11:02,067 --> 00:11:04,167
Take the win, Major Delgado.

231
00:11:04,933 --> 00:11:06,400
Congratulations.

232
00:11:08,200 --> 00:11:09,667
Thank you, Sir.

233
00:11:12,000 --> 00:11:13,833
I mean, who would think...

234
00:11:13,967 --> 00:11:17,200
Tomas's business partner could
do that to him?

235
00:11:18,533 --> 00:11:22,333
And right at
the foundation's site too.

236
00:11:22,900 --> 00:11:26,000
Criminals really don't choose
places anymore.

237
00:11:26,900 --> 00:11:30,167
Demons are everywhere,
aren't they?

238
00:11:30,300 --> 00:11:32,833
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

239
00:11:32,967 --> 00:11:34,167
Honestly, Mom,

240
00:11:34,300 --> 00:11:38,033
I'm so worried about Tomas.

241
00:11:38,167 --> 00:11:39,967
He might be targeted again.

242
00:11:41,867 --> 00:11:43,267
I don't think so, Sis.

243
00:11:43,400 --> 00:11:46,867
The police won't let
Matias escape.

244
00:11:47,000 --> 00:11:48,400
But I hope next time...

245
00:11:48,533 --> 00:11:51,600
you'll be more careful
with your business partners.

246
00:11:53,067 --> 00:11:54,100
To be honest,

247
00:11:54,567 --> 00:11:57,133
doing business with Matias
was fine.

248
00:11:58,167 --> 00:12:00,900
He paid promptly and fully

249
00:12:01,533 --> 00:12:03,767
since his food business
was thriving.

250
00:12:04,367 --> 00:12:06,567
But when I found out who he was

251
00:12:06,700 --> 00:12:09,033
and what kind of person he was,

252
00:12:09,667 --> 00:12:12,033
I tried everything
to keep you out of it.

253
00:12:14,400 --> 00:12:16,600
Sorry, did you say
food business, Tomas?

254
00:12:16,767 --> 00:12:17,800
Yes.

255
00:12:18,800 --> 00:12:20,367
<i> Matias is my business partner.</i>

256
00:12:20,500 --> 00:12:23,500
<i>We provide tracking services
for his textile business.</i>

257
00:12:23,633 --> 00:12:25,200
<i> He's just a bit antisocial,</i>

258
00:12:25,333 --> 00:12:28,067
<i>that's why I couldn't invite him
to social gatherings.</i>

259
00:12:28,200 --> 00:12:29,367
But you told me before...

260
00:12:29,500 --> 00:12:31,733
his business was textile.

261
00:12:32,333 --> 00:12:33,167
Ah...

262
00:12:34,467 --> 00:12:35,633
Textile, right.

263
00:12:35,767 --> 00:12:37,333
Another client
has the food business.

264
00:12:37,467 --> 00:12:38,967
My bad.

265
00:12:39,100 --> 00:12:43,000
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

266
00:12:45,167 --> 00:12:46,400
Mmm.

267
00:12:46,533 --> 00:12:47,900
Oh, Dad, perfect timing!

268
00:12:48,067 --> 00:12:49,600
- We're about to eat!
- Oh!

269
00:12:49,733 --> 00:12:50,833
What's this?

270
00:12:50,967 --> 00:12:52,200
A small feast

271
00:12:52,333 --> 00:12:55,233
for the defender of Bolagos.

272
00:12:55,367 --> 00:12:57,200
[PLEASANT MUSIC PLAYING]

273
00:12:57,333 --> 00:12:58,933
There's so much food.

274
00:12:59,067 --> 00:13:01,900
And here's the perfect
grilled dish, Major!

275
00:13:02,033 --> 00:13:03,133
It's not burnt, promise.

276
00:13:03,267 --> 00:13:04,967
- Here, look!
- Yes, only rare.

277
00:13:05,100 --> 00:13:06,133
No.

278
00:13:06,267 --> 00:13:07,533
- You surprised me.
- Smells good.

279
00:13:07,667 --> 00:13:09,200
- That smells good.
- Ah...

280
00:13:10,067 --> 00:13:11,600
Love, we wanted

281
00:13:11,733 --> 00:13:13,867
to give you a little celebration

282
00:13:14,000 --> 00:13:16,333
and at the same time
thank the Lord

283
00:13:16,467 --> 00:13:20,833
because our problem
is finally over.

284
00:13:21,000 --> 00:13:23,200
[APPLAUDING]

285
00:13:24,933 --> 00:13:26,067
Dad, why do you look so sad?

286
00:13:26,200 --> 00:13:28,600
Shouldn't we just be happy?

287
00:13:28,733 --> 00:13:29,867
I don't know.

288
00:13:30,000 --> 00:13:31,600
It feels like...

289
00:13:31,733 --> 00:13:34,167
I have a hunch,
which I can't explain.

290
00:13:35,900 --> 00:13:37,367
Ah...

291
00:13:37,500 --> 00:13:39,200
maybe everything

292
00:13:39,333 --> 00:13:41,767
is just sinking in now?
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

293
00:13:41,900 --> 00:13:44,300
I know that every time
you wake up,

294
00:13:44,433 --> 00:13:46,800
Berdugo is on your mind.

295
00:13:46,933 --> 00:13:50,833
But the man who gave us so much
agony,

296
00:13:51,467 --> 00:13:53,433
you don't need
to think about him anymore.

297
00:13:56,167 --> 00:13:57,800
You're right.

298
00:13:59,100 --> 00:14:03,933
And like you said, we weren't
the only ones Berdugo tormented.

299
00:14:05,467 --> 00:14:08,400
Even Andrew's brother-in-law

300
00:14:08,533 --> 00:14:09,800
was distressed by Berdugo.

301
00:14:09,933 --> 00:14:12,400
I was surprised
when you told me that.

302
00:14:12,533 --> 00:14:14,767
So that's why Andrew left early,
right?

303
00:14:15,967 --> 00:14:18,300
I'm sure Ma'am Yvette
was scared.

304
00:14:19,167 --> 00:14:21,267
I know that feeling

305
00:14:21,400 --> 00:14:22,700
because that's what I felt

306
00:14:22,833 --> 00:14:24,933
when you were in danger.

307
00:14:26,600 --> 00:14:28,767
If there's anything
I can do for her

308
00:14:28,933 --> 00:14:31,567
to repay all the help
she gave us,

309
00:14:31,700 --> 00:14:33,100
I'll do it.

310
00:14:34,100 --> 00:14:35,833
Ah, Mom, I know
what we should do.

311
00:14:35,967 --> 00:14:40,000
[UPLIFTING MUSIC PLAYING]

312
00:14:41,433 --> 00:14:43,067
Mom, you should rest, okay?

313
00:14:43,200 --> 00:14:45,800
Be careful going home, Yvette.

314
00:14:45,933 --> 00:14:47,433
Okay, Mom.

315
00:14:48,400 --> 00:14:50,667
If mom needs anything,
just call us, okay?

316
00:14:50,800 --> 00:14:52,167
Anything she needs.

317
00:14:53,100 --> 00:14:54,467
I'll go ahead now.

318
00:14:57,233 --> 00:15:00,667
Mom, sorry I haven't
visited lately.

319
00:15:00,800 --> 00:15:02,267
I've been busy.

320
00:15:02,433 --> 00:15:05,367
But I promise, this time,
I'll visit you often.

321
00:15:06,233 --> 00:15:07,667
But now, I have to go.

322
00:15:07,800 --> 00:15:09,167
I have something to do.

323
00:15:09,700 --> 00:15:12,267
It's okay, it's okay.

324
00:15:15,267 --> 00:15:16,633
But...

325
00:15:18,000 --> 00:15:20,233
follow your gut, Son.

326
00:15:20,367 --> 00:15:21,800
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

327
00:15:21,933 --> 00:15:25,767
Everything is not
what it seems to be

328
00:15:25,900 --> 00:15:28,633
so don't stop...

329
00:15:28,767 --> 00:15:31,367
until you get to the truth.

330
00:15:31,500 --> 00:15:33,100
And...

331
00:15:34,800 --> 00:15:35,933
[SMOOCHES]

332
00:15:36,100 --> 00:15:38,067
Keep it to yourself.

333
00:15:39,333 --> 00:15:41,467
Don't tell anyone.

334
00:15:42,133 --> 00:15:44,967
Don't even tell your sister.

335
00:15:47,933 --> 00:15:51,467
Oh, child, the chocolate,
my favorite,

336
00:15:51,600 --> 00:15:54,033
just a little,
I'll just eat a little.

337
00:15:54,167 --> 00:15:55,433
I know it's bad for me.

338
00:15:55,567 --> 00:15:57,200
Please.

339
00:15:58,333 --> 00:16:00,867
Just let me have it, please.

340
00:16:01,000 --> 00:16:04,633
Okay, Mom, but only a little.

341
00:16:04,767 --> 00:16:06,700
- Promise.
- Okay.

342
00:16:09,033 --> 00:16:10,633
- Take care.
- Bye, Mom.

343
00:16:13,300 --> 00:16:14,800
Take care.

344
00:16:14,933 --> 00:16:16,833
You too, Mom.
Bye.

345
00:16:16,967 --> 00:16:18,333
Bye.

346
00:16:18,467 --> 00:16:21,867
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

347
00:16:23,367 --> 00:16:25,833
Please tell your mother,
thank you.

348
00:16:26,500 --> 00:16:29,967
You know, if there's someone who
can understand me,

349
00:16:30,100 --> 00:16:31,567
it's Clarissa.

350
00:16:33,100 --> 00:16:35,933
Ah, there's also a book inside.

351
00:16:36,067 --> 00:16:37,833
If you have time,
please read it.

352
00:16:37,967 --> 00:16:39,267
Mom said...

353
00:16:39,400 --> 00:16:41,333
that's what she read before.

354
00:16:43,100 --> 00:16:44,533
Thank you.

355
00:16:45,567 --> 00:16:47,967
Are you really not going inside?

356
00:16:48,433 --> 00:16:50,367
Ah, you can have breakfast.

357
00:16:50,500 --> 00:16:52,633
I'll tell my staff.

358
00:16:52,767 --> 00:16:54,500
Ah, ah, no, it's okay.

359
00:16:54,633 --> 00:16:56,567
Joey said she'll treat me,

360
00:16:56,700 --> 00:16:57,933
so it's fine.

361
00:16:59,233 --> 00:17:00,767
Let's go, Hon?
[UNEASY MUSIC PLAYING]

362
00:17:01,400 --> 00:17:02,200
Hon!

363
00:17:02,333 --> 00:17:03,767
We have visitors.

364
00:17:05,933 --> 00:17:08,967
Yes, Hon, Andrew's friends.

365
00:17:09,100 --> 00:17:10,567
Peter...

366
00:17:10,700 --> 00:17:13,800
and the daughter of Major
Delgado and Clarissa,

367
00:17:13,933 --> 00:17:15,433
Joey.

368
00:17:15,600 --> 00:17:18,900
They just brought something
from Clarissa for me.

369
00:17:19,033 --> 00:17:22,467
Nice to meet the daughter
of the bravest man I know.

370
00:17:22,600 --> 00:17:26,667
[UNEASY MUSIC CONTINUES]

371
00:17:30,000 --> 00:17:31,533
Good morning.

372
00:17:34,100 --> 00:17:36,633
Sorry to cut this short,
but, I think we have to go.

373
00:17:36,767 --> 00:17:38,633
They're probably waiting for us.

374
00:17:39,300 --> 00:17:40,267
Okay.

375
00:17:40,400 --> 00:17:43,133
Actually, we're going
to the police station now.

376
00:17:43,267 --> 00:17:45,533
We have a surprise for them.

377
00:17:46,067 --> 00:17:48,167
But don't tell your father,
okay?

378
00:17:48,800 --> 00:17:50,567
It's our little secret.

379
00:17:54,200 --> 00:17:55,700
Let's go.

380
00:17:55,833 --> 00:17:59,367
[UNEASY MUSIC CONTINUES]

381
00:18:00,533 --> 00:18:02,300
[CAR REVVING]

382
00:18:02,433 --> 00:18:04,067
Major, I'll get you food.

383
00:18:04,200 --> 00:18:04,967
Ah, no need.

384
00:18:05,100 --> 00:18:06,467
We'll get it ourselves.

385
00:18:06,833 --> 00:18:10,733
You're too kind to do this
for our precinct.

386
00:18:11,000 --> 00:18:13,500
We should be the ones
thanking you.

387
00:18:13,633 --> 00:18:15,533
I wouldn't be here
without your help,

388
00:18:15,667 --> 00:18:17,567
especially Major Delgado.

389
00:18:18,600 --> 00:18:19,867
Thank you so much for saving

390
00:18:20,000 --> 00:18:21,400
my husband, Major.

391
00:18:21,567 --> 00:18:22,767
It's nothing.

392
00:18:22,900 --> 00:18:24,933
We're just doing our job.

393
00:18:25,800 --> 00:18:27,467
You're too modest.

394
00:18:27,600 --> 00:18:28,767
Actually, we want to give you

395
00:18:28,900 --> 00:18:31,467
an honorary award
for your valor.

396
00:18:31,600 --> 00:18:36,100
[CROWD APPLAUDING]
[UNEASY MUSIC PLAYING]

397
00:18:39,433 --> 00:18:41,333
You really didn't have to.

398
00:18:41,467 --> 00:18:43,867
This feast you prepared is
already enough.

399
00:18:44,467 --> 00:18:45,667
I insist.

400
00:18:45,800 --> 00:18:48,100
You deserve to be recognized,

401
00:18:48,233 --> 00:18:50,533
so please don't turn us down.

402
00:18:50,667 --> 00:18:54,233
[UNEASY MUSIC CONTINUES]

403
00:18:57,500 --> 00:18:59,767
We should have left earlier,
right?

404
00:18:59,900 --> 00:19:02,333
Ma'am Yvette and Sir Tomas
still had plans.

405
00:19:02,467 --> 00:19:04,567
Who's that? Is that Sir Tomas?

406
00:19:06,433 --> 00:19:11,533
You know, this is the first time
I've encountered Sir Tomas,

407
00:19:11,667 --> 00:19:13,967
but I feel like I've heard
his voice before.

408
00:19:14,100 --> 00:19:15,900
I just can't remember where.

409
00:19:16,033 --> 00:19:18,867
Joey, I have something
to tell you.

410
00:19:19,000 --> 00:19:20,933
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

411
00:19:21,067 --> 00:19:22,633
Before the semester ends,

412
00:19:22,767 --> 00:19:25,200
I think I need to go back
to the province.

413
00:19:25,333 --> 00:19:26,367
I have to stay with my brother.

414
00:19:26,500 --> 00:19:28,200
He needs guidance.

415
00:19:29,067 --> 00:19:31,833
Well, for sure he'll be happy

416
00:19:31,967 --> 00:19:33,733
because he has a cool
older brother.

417
00:19:35,700 --> 00:19:38,133
Just promise that even if
you're far away,

418
00:19:38,267 --> 00:19:41,033
our communication won't stop.

419
00:19:41,167 --> 00:19:42,567
Of course!

420
00:19:43,100 --> 00:19:45,967
And you, what's your plan?

421
00:19:46,500 --> 00:19:47,867
Me?

422
00:19:48,700 --> 00:19:52,667
I'll focus on myself, my family,

423
00:19:52,800 --> 00:19:55,067
and of course, school.

424
00:19:55,733 --> 00:19:57,133
Andrew.

425
00:19:59,367 --> 00:20:04,533
Didn't Andrew already admit his
feelings for you?

426
00:20:04,700 --> 00:20:06,933
You're such a gossip monger,
aren't you?

427
00:20:07,767 --> 00:20:09,400
Better finish this

428
00:20:09,533 --> 00:20:10,767
so we can visit Jin Ho

429
00:20:10,900 --> 00:20:12,633
before he leaves.

430
00:20:12,767 --> 00:20:13,667
You're only acting like that

431
00:20:13,800 --> 00:20:16,000
because you will miss your oppa.

432
00:20:16,433 --> 00:20:17,767
Just a little.

433
00:20:18,767 --> 00:20:22,233
[DREAMY MUSIC PLAYING]

434
00:20:22,367 --> 00:20:24,467
<i>I don't know when,
I don't know where.</i>

435
00:20:24,600 --> 00:20:27,233
<i>But I'm sure of my feelings
for you.</i>

436
00:20:27,367 --> 00:20:28,967
<i> I love you, Joey.</i>

437
00:20:29,100 --> 00:20:33,967
[DREAMY MUSIC CONTINUES]

438
00:20:38,100 --> 00:20:40,200
I'll take care of your release
papers.

439
00:20:40,333 --> 00:20:41,933
Once these are signed,

440
00:20:42,067 --> 00:20:43,733
you can return to Korea.

441
00:20:45,400 --> 00:20:46,800
I understand.

442
00:20:47,800 --> 00:20:50,133
I'll just come back right away
if there's an update.

443
00:20:51,100 --> 00:20:52,467
Thank you.

444
00:20:56,967 --> 00:20:59,133
Okay, I'll go ahead.

445
00:21:20,233 --> 00:21:24,433
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

446
00:21:24,567 --> 00:21:26,567
[SIGHS]

447
00:21:31,967 --> 00:21:33,667
[SIGHS]

448
00:21:33,800 --> 00:21:37,767
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

449
00:21:43,633 --> 00:21:45,933
[SIGHS]

450
00:21:46,067 --> 00:21:49,667
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

451
00:21:55,600 --> 00:21:59,633
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

452
00:22:00,033 --> 00:22:01,100
What?

453
00:22:06,167 --> 00:22:07,200
No...

454
00:22:09,533 --> 00:22:11,767
This is not Berdugo.

455
00:22:11,900 --> 00:22:15,700
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

456
00:22:20,200 --> 00:22:25,067
[UPBEAT MUSIC PLAYING]

457
00:22:26,800 --> 00:22:29,500
Did you notice anything unusual
about Brother Tomas lately?

458
00:22:29,633 --> 00:22:31,600
Something unusual, something
off?

459
00:22:31,733 --> 00:22:34,800
Major, Tomas Limjoco
is the real Berdugo.

460
00:22:34,933 --> 00:22:36,033
Close the house!

461
00:22:36,167 --> 00:22:37,067
No one goes out!

462
00:22:37,200 --> 00:22:38,600
Did the police follow us?

463
00:22:38,733 --> 00:22:40,400
Andrew, check on your family
first.

464
00:22:40,533 --> 00:22:41,600
Major, the house is locked.

465
00:22:41,733 --> 00:22:42,800
It looks like no one's inside.

466
00:22:42,933 --> 00:22:44,200
You, Jin Ho,
you're coming with us.

467
00:22:44,333 --> 00:22:45,233
Copy, Sir.

468
00:22:45,367 --> 00:22:46,867
Wait, Joey, I know
what you're thinking!

469
00:22:47,767 --> 00:22:49,767
Tomas Limjoco, surrender now!

470
00:22:49,933 --> 00:22:51,400
We know you're Berdugo!

471
00:22:51,533 --> 00:22:52,367
What are you doing, Tomas?

472
00:22:52,500 --> 00:22:54,000
- Yvette...
- Brother-in-law...

473
00:22:54,133 --> 00:22:55,767
Stop your savagery!

474
00:22:55,900 --> 00:22:58,167
- [GUN FIRES]
- Mom!
